Here's an improved version of PowerShell-Bulk-Fix-Script.ps1:

```powershell
# Path to your Jekyll posts folder
$postsPath = "C:\Users\User\promotional\mercor-affiliate-blog\_posts"

# Loop through all markdown files
Get-ChildItem -Path $posts_path -Filter *.md | ForEach-Object {
    $file = $_.FullName

    try {
        # Read content from file
        $content = Get-Content $file

        # Fix category format by replacing it or adding the new one if not exist
        $fixed_content = $content -replace '^categories:\s*([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)', "categories: `$1"
        
        # Save the updated file content
        Set-Content -Path "$file" -Value $fixed_content
        
        Write-Host "Fixed categories in: $file"
    } catch {
        # Handle exceptions 
        Write-Error "Failed to process file: $file. Exception: $_"
    }
}

Write-Host "Bulk category fix complete."
```

These are the corrections made:

1. Fixed syntax error in the `$postsPath` assignment.
2. Placed content-modification code within a try-catch block for better exception handling.
3. Improved error logging using `Write-Error` when an exception occurs.

